# ARC ESP fix workflow (MANDATORY)

**Every agent session in this repo MUST follow this protocol for ESP work.** Do not skip steps. Do not batch fixes. Do not guess pipeline stage. Reference docs live in [`help/`](help/README.md).

## The loop (every single change)

```
ONE CHANGE → KILL EXE → BUILD → RUN → TEST ALL 4 → REPORT → DECIDE NEXT
```

1. **One focused change** — smallest diff that tests one hypothesis. **Never** stack unrelated fixes in one build.
2. **Kill → build → run** from project root after **every** change:
   ```powershell
   .\rebuild-run.ps1          # full cycle (default)
   .\rebuild-run.ps1 -BuildOnly
   .\rebuild-run.ps1 -RunOnly
   ```
   Manual kill if needed: `Get-Process -Name "ArcRaiders" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force`
3. **Tell the user exactly what to check** (all four areas below) before they test.
4. **Wait for structured 4-area report** — even when only bots changed. Do not start the next edit until user reports.
5. **Use debug overlay** — menu **Show offset validation** (`var::show_debug_overlay`). Read console tags; **do not guess** which pipeline stage failed.

## What to test every time (all four)

| Area | Menu tab | Pass criteria |
|---|---|---|
| **Players** | Player ESP | Boxes, names, health, skeleton, distance — no regressions |
| **Bots** | Bot ESP | Real names (Wasp, Pop, Surveyor…), no "ARC"/"Oil"/"Bot" placeholders, no self-as-bot, no ghost bots |
| **Items** | Item/loot ESP | Correct loot labels, distance filter, no bots mislabeled as items |
| **World** | Container/world ESP | Crates, containers, props with correct categories |

## Required report format (user pastes after each test)

```
Players:   OK | broken — (detail)
Bots:      OK | broken | none — (detail)
Items:     OK | broken | none — (detail)
World:     OK | broken | none — (detail)
Debug:     on | off
  [debugPlayer] ...
  [debugRobot] ...
  [debugItem] ...
  [debugContainer] ...
```

## Debug overlay (ground truth)

| Tag | File | Key fields |
|---|---|---|
| `[debugPlayer]` | `EntityList.cpp` | `scanned`, `admitted`, `drawing`, `cache`, `dedup`, `posSkip`, `posFail`, `rootStale`, `nameFail`, `weaponHit`, `weaponScan`, `ghostEvict`, `healthZero` |
| `[debugRobot]` | `RobotList.cpp` | `scanned`, `admitted`, `drawing`, `cache`, `structHit`, `fnameHit`, `visSkip`, `distSkip`, `zeroPos`, `enemyCount` |
| `[debugItem]` | `ItemList.cpp` | `scanned`, `admitted`, `depleted`, `denyReAdmit`, `ttlEvict`, `posSkip`, `drawing`, `cache`, `pickedHidden`, `pickedSearched`, `pickedNoDa`, `pickedNoCol`, `pickedSpawnEmpty`, `pickedStillId` |
| `[debugContainer]` | `ContainerList.cpp` | `scanned`, `admitted`, `preSkip`, `structHit`, `admitLooks`, `admitGate`, `rootSkip`, `posSkip`, `drawing`, `opened`, `unopened`, `openSalvage`, `openItemContainer`, `openSearched`, `cache` |
| `[debugAim]` | `Aimbot.cpp` | `frameOk`, `candidates`, `locked`, `dx`, `dy`, `gain`, `grace`, `kmbox`, `skipDraw` |

**Item debug reads:** `depleted`/`ttlEvict` high → pickup eviction firing; `denyReAdmit` high → blink fix blocking re-admit; `pickedStillId` high + other picked* 0 → asset ID lingers but no strong signal (offset probe cycle); `drawing` > 0 after pickup → check `[debugWorldEsp] skipPickedUp` render safety net.

**Container debug reads:** `preSkip` high → failed `QuickContainerCandidate`; `structHit` high + `admitted` 0 → pre-filter passed but both `looksLikeContainer` and `AdmitContainerActor` failed; `admitLooks` vs `admitGate` → which admission path won; `opened` high but `openSalvage`/`openItemContainer`/`openSearched` all 0 → open detection offset probe needed; `cache` > 0 but nothing on screen → render/collect path in `Esp.cpp`.

**Bot debug reads:** `structHit` high + `admitted` 0 → QuickBotCandidate passed but `VerifyBotActor` failed; `fnameHit` high → `ResolveBotDrawLabel` empty at draw; `admitted` high + `drawing` 0 → position/distance/vis filters; `zeroPos` high → position reads failing; `cache` > 0 but nothing on screen → render/collect path in `Esp.cpp`; `enemyCount` vs `cache` → sanity only (not admission).

**Player debug reads:** `drawing` > 0 but ESP frozen at spawn → check `rootStale`/`posFail`; `nameFail` high → decrypt/offset probe (`SteamDecrypt.hpp`); `weaponScan` 0 + all Unarmed → weapon class pattern mismatch (enable **Show weapon**); `ghostEvict` rising → stale-position / self-PS filter working; `healthZero` high → `HealthInfo` @ PS+0x530 miss (fallback `get_health` path).

**Aim debug reads:** `frameOk=0` → frame builder not running / not in raid; `candidates=0` with players visible → eligibility, FOV, or vis check; large `dx`/`dy` + `kmbox=0` → hardware not initialized; `grace=1` + aim at empty space → stale sticky position (disable grace to test); `skipDraw` high → targets beyond ESP distance but inside aim distance (should still aim after A+ fix).

## Coupling — why fixes break other ESP

Shared code affects **all** scanners. Before editing any shared function, **grep all callers** and note impact on bots + items + world. See [`help/SHARED_GATES.md`](help/SHARED_GATES.md).

| Shared choke point | Used by |
|---|---|
| `getEntityType()` | Bots, loot, world classification |
| `getAllowType()` | Bot/item/world admission |
| `IsAcceptedBotEspLabel()` | Bot admission + render validation |
| `HumanizeActorFName()`, `ResolveWorldLabel()`, `LookupByAssetName()` | Naming everywhere |
| `WorldScanCommon` helpers | All scanners |

**Durable bot fix:** use bot-only resolvers in `RobotList.cpp` / `AssetNames.cpp` — **do not** widen shared item/world naming gates.

## Frozen vs touchable files

| Category | Files | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| **Frozen** | `Project/Functions/EntityList.cpp`, player collect/render in `Project/Functions/Esp.cpp` | Do not edit unless fixing players |
| **Bot work** | `RobotList.cpp`, `RobotList.h`, bot render in `Esp.cpp`, `EspDraw.h` | Bot-only fixes |
| **Items/world** | `ItemList.cpp`, `ContainerList.cpp`, `World.cpp` | Loot/container fixes |
| **Shared** (grep callers first) | `Utils.cpp`, `AssetNames.cpp`, `WorldScanCommon.cpp` | Never widen gates for bot fixes |

## Bot naming (no placeholders)

Never use "ARC", "Bot", "Oil". Resolve real names via (priority order):
1. Actor class fname → runtime bot token map from `Bots_Items_Maps/en.json` + `getEntityType()`
2. `GetEnemyTypeDataAssetFName()` at `0x11A0` / `0x1190`
3. Skeletal mesh fname
4. `LookupEnemyBotByFName()` / `Bots_Items_Maps`

Never fall back to generic item asset names (`DA_Item_*`) for bots.

## Recommended fix order

1. Baseline — user reports all four + debug numbers (no code changes)
2. Isolate bot naming — bot-only resolvers; stop routing bots through shared item/world naming
3. Bot admission → bot render → bot smoothing (without touching player code)
4. Items/world — only if regressed; fix in item/world files, not by widening shared gates

## Git / GitHub

- **Do not push to GitHub** unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Do not commit** unless the user asks for a local checkpoint.

## Cursor modes

| Situation | Mode |
|---|---|
| Multi-step fix, scope lock before edits | **Plan** |
| One change, build, run, test | **Agent** |
| Explain code, no edits | **Ask** |
| Runtime numbers + user report needed | **Agent** + debug overlay on |

There is no separate "debug mode." Debugging = Agent + overlay + structured report.

